      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-7{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{3}=-{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={b}_{1}+10{b}_{2}-7{b}_{3} \\\\  & =-7{b}_{3}+10{b}_{2}+{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-7{b}_{3}+5(2{b}_{2})-(-{b}_{1}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}+5{c}_{2}-{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$",
